2026-10-21T22:44:40.3209185Z | original / unrelated-definition | 0.099007 | 0.072662 | 26.61% | 5/5 | [0.68943,0.78451] | SPEEDUP |
2026-10-21T22:44:40.3210087Z | expanded / early-definition | 0.415131 | 0.386271 | 6.95% | 5/5 | [0.51822,0.96830] | SPEEDUP |
2026-10-21T22:44:40.3211057Z | expanded / unrelated-definition | 0.372622 | 0.385291 | -3.40% | 3/5 | [0.48449,1.05316] | NO_SPEEDUP |
2026-10-21T22:44:40.3211635Z 
2026-10-21T22:44:40.3212389Z CPU, all phase/resource observations, same-input direct Rust comparisons, cold replay and representative full witnesses are preserved in the JSON reports.
2026-10-21T22:44:40.3213765Z NO_SPEEDUP is a valid economic result and does not change the independent correctness qualification.
2026-10-21T22:44:40.3214866Z Frozen bounded tests do not formally prove the retained parser bridge or qualify a multi-update lifetime.
